<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aleuas the Red</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> · Also known as Aleuas Pyrrhos</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aleuas the Red was a semi-legendary ruler of Larissa in the 6th century BCE, ancestor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleuadae">Aleuadae</a>, the leading aristocratic family of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaly">Thessaly</a>. He was credited with dividing Thessaly into four districts, the tetrads, and with fixing the cavalry and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoplite">hoplites</a> each district owed, the basis of the Thessalian League's military organisation.</p></div>
